  "active_proposal_id": "P024",
  "reason": "P024 is the only option that addresses the fundamental problem of governance: establishing a bridge between abstract community fear and verifiable, pre-deployment reality. While C01, C04, and C05 focus on the mechanics of attestation and the risk of gaming the system, they all assume a 'fear' framework that P024 explicitly critiques as being based on 'extrapolation rather than direct observation.' P024 is the most rigorous because it demands empirical, pre-deployment evidence to satisfy a majority of parties, which is the only way to move from speculative risk management to actionable, verifiable governance. It forces the system to define what 'capable' or 'unsafe' actually looks like in a measurable way before deployment, rather than relying on the static checklists of P022/P023 which are inherently vulnerable to the optimization/gaming problems highlighted in the candidates. P024 is the only one that seeks to resolve the 'fear' itself through data."
}

